  "architectural_findings": [
    "Homepage is presentation-layer accumulation rather than a single V2 design system.",
    "Two discovery runtimes coexist: Commerce Discovery V1 and AI Discovery V2.",
    "AI Discovery V2 currently behaves as governed natural-language search; a structured intent/journey layer is not yet a separate runtime contract.",
    "home-v5.js injects runtime header CSS, including !important overrides, creating a second styling authority.",
    "Legacy header generations coexist with final-header bootstrap/entry/init files and page-level header contracts.",
    "Existing tests encode V5/premium-V1 assumptions that must be migrated before those generations can be retired.",
    "The canonical 34-basket registry product-taxonomy.js is a strong KEEP boundary.",
    "server.js preserves the frontend-to-canonical-API boundary and rejects local /api routes with canonical_api_only."
  ],
